**Risks:**
- These changes change the behavior from raising an exception (which might trigger Celery retries) to silently exiting if the user is not found. Given that the user no longer exists, retrying is unlikely to resolve the issue, so this is the correct approach to prevent unnecessary error noise in Sentry.
