The issue was caused by the `receive_loop` in `TCPROSTransport` attempting to reconnect even when the remote end had closed the connection (resulting in an empty read). In such cases, `recv_buff` would raise a `TransportTerminated` exception. Because the loop caught `TransportException` and proceeded to attempt reconnection, it entered an infinite loop of failed reconnection attempts with exponential backoff, causing the observed 32-second delay and wasted ports.

I modified `TCPROSTransport.receive_loop` in `clients/rospy/src/rospy/impl/tcpros_base.py` to check if the caught `TransportException` is an instance of `TransportTerminated`. If it is, the loop now breaks immediately instead of attempting to reconnect, matching the behavior of the C++ implementation where receiving zero bytes results in closing the connection and stopping.

