The issue is caused by the `list_to_class` method in `src/bootstrap4/renderers.py`, which assumes that every `<label>` element inside the enclosing `div` contains an `<input>` element as a direct child (accessible via `label.input`). When a label does not contain an input, `label.input` is `None`, leading to an `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'attrs'` when attempting to access its attributes.

To fix this, I added a check to ensure `label.input` is not `None` before attempting to access its attributes and apply the Bootstrap class.

```python
def list_to_class(self, html, klass):
    # ... (previous code)
    enclosing_div = soup.find("div", {"class": classes})
    if enclosing_div:
        for label in enclosing_div.find_all("label"):
            label.attrs["class"] = label.attrs.get("class", []) + ["form-check-label"]
            if label.input:
                label.input.attrs["class"] = label.input.attrs.get("class", []) + ["form-check-input"]
    return str(soup)
```

