The issue was caused by a regression in `FieldRenderer.list_to_class` in `src/bootstrap4/renderers.py`. The code assumed that every `<label>` tag found within a specific container would have an `<input>` tag as a direct attribute (`label.input`), which is not necessarily true in valid HTML. This led to an `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'attrs'` when a label did not contain an input.

I fixed this by using `label.find("input")` to safely locate the input tag and checking if it exists before attempting to access its attributes and add the `form-check-input` class.

```python
    def list_to_class(self, html, klass):
        # ... (lines 323-339)
        if enclosing_div:
            for label in enclosing_div.find_all("label"):
                label.attrs["class"] = label.attrs.get("class", []) + ["form-check-label"]
                input_tag = label.find("input")
                if input_tag:
                    input_tag.attrs["class"] = input_tag.attrs.get("class", []) + ["form-check-input"]
        return str(soup)
```

