The problem was caused by an infinite recursion loop in `PlotItem.setDownsampling`. When calling this method programmatically, it updated the UI controls (like checkboxes and radio buttons) using `setChecked()`. These UI updates triggered signals that were connected to `updateDownsampling()`, which in turn called `setDownsampling()` on each curve, re-triggering the cycle.

I fixed this by adding checks to ensure that UI control states are only updated (via `setChecked` or `setValue`) if they actually differ from the requested state. This prevents the emission of signals when no logical change in the UI occurs, thereby breaking the infinite loop.

