The issue was caused by an unnecessary wait in the `fill_select` function within `cfme/web_ui/__init__.py`. Specifically, after the selection was made via `sel.select(slist, val)`, the code called `slist.observer_wait()`, which could take a significant amount of time (up to 120 seconds as seen in the logs) if the expected observer event did not fire or was already satisfied.

I have removed the `slist.observer_wait()` call in `cfme/web_ui/__init__.py` to allow the automation to proceed immediately after the dropdown value is selected, thereby resolving the performance bottleneck when filling forms with dropdown menus.

```python
@fill.method((Select, types.NoneType))
@fill.method((Select, object))
def fill_select(slist, val):
    logger.debug('  Filling in {} with value {}'.format(str(slist), val))
    prev_sel = sel.select(slist, val)
    return prev_sel
```

The issue was caused by an unnecessary call to `slist.observer_wait()` in the `fill_select` function within `cfme/web_ui/__init__.py`. This call waited for an observer event that might not fire immediately or at all, leading to significant delays (up to 120 seconds as shown in the logs) when filling dropdown menus.

I have removed the `slist.observer_wait()` call from `fill_select` to allow the automation to proceed immediately after the selection is made, resolving the performance bottleneck.

```python
@fill.method((Select, types.NoneType))
@fill.method((Select, object))
def fill_select(slist, val):
    logger.debug('  Filling in {} with value {}'.format(str(slist), val))
    prev_sel = sel.select(slist, val)
    return prev_sel
```

