The issue was caused by a call to `slist.observer_wait()` in the `fill_select` method within `cfme/web_ui/__init__.py`. This method caused the automation to wait for a UI change that might not have occurred as expected, leading to significant delays (often around 120 seconds) and timeouts during form filling.

I fixed this by removing the `slist.observer_wait()` call, allowing the automation to proceed immediately after the selection is made.

```python
@fill.method((Select, types.NoneType))
@fill.method((Select, object))
def fill_select(slist, val):
    logger.debug('  Filling in {} with value {}'.format(str(slist), val))
    return sel.select(slist, val)
```

This change resolves the reported issue where filling forms with dropdowns was taking an excessively long time.

The issue where filling forms with dropdowns takes a long time was caused by an unnecessary `slist.observer_wait()` call in the `fill_select` function. The logs indicated that this method was timing out (waiting for up to 120 seconds) while trying to wait for an element that was either not appearing as expected or no longer present, even though the selection itself had already been successfully performed by `sel.select(slist, val)`.

I have removed the `slist.observer_wait()` call from `fill_select` in `cfme/web_ui/__init__.py`. This allows the automation to proceed immediately after a successful selection, resolving the long delays described in the issue.

```python
@fill.method((Select, types.NoneType))
@fill.method((Select, object))
def fill_select(slist, val):
    logger.debug('  Filling in {} with value {}'.format(str(slist), val))
    prev_sel = sel.select(slist, val)
    return prev_sel
```

