workers.report:
The issue was that picking an option from a dropdown menu was taking an excessive amount of time because the `fill_select` method in `cfme/web_ui/__init__.py` was calling `slist.observer_wait()` after the selection was made. This caused the automation to wait for an observer to trigger, which often resulted in long timeouts (around 120 seconds) when the condition was not met as expected.

I fixed this by removing the `slist.observer_wait()` call from the `fill_select` method, allowing the method to return immediately after the selection is performed.

```python
@fill.method((Select, types.NoneType))
@fill.method((Select, object))
def fill_select(slist, val):
    logger.debug('  Filling in {} with value {}'.format(str(slist), val))
    prev_sel = sel.select(slist, val)
    return prev_sel
