The issue was caused by an unhandled exception during the network request in the `alive` method of the `DeadMansSwitchClient` model. Specifically, `urllib2.urlopen` could raise various exceptions (e.g., `URLError`, `HTTPError`, `TimeoutError`) if the configured server was unreachable or returned an error, causing the entire process (such as a Runbot worker) to crash.

I have fixed this by wrapping the `urllib2.urlopen` call in a `try-except` block to catch any exceptions. If an error occurs, it is now logged as an error instead of allowing the exception to propagate and crash the process.

```python
    @api.model
