The issue was that launching EC2 instances using the `ec2_instance.py` module could fail when AWS encountered insufficient capacity for the requested instance type in the specified Availability Zone (`InsufficientInstanceCapacity`). The current implementation used the default boto3 retry logic, which was insufficient for these types of transient capacity issues.

